<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prusias I of Bithynia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 243–182 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a> · Also known as Prusias I Cholus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prusias I was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bithynia">Bithynia</a> from about 228 to 182 BCE. He expanded the kingdom at the expense of its neighbours, fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> in 220 BCE over its tolls on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> shipping and warred with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pergamon">Pergamon</a>. He founded the city of Prusa, modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bursa">Bursa</a>, and gave refuge to the Carthaginian general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a>, who served him as a commander before taking poison to avoid being handed over to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prusias-i-of-bithynia.jpg" alt="Prusias I of Bithynia" width="320" height="322" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: PHGCOM · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prusias_I_of_Bithynia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
